<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KOCOPIA seeks 52,500T of U.S. corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KOCOPIA seeks 52,500T of U.S. corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Corn Processing Industry Association (KOCOPIA) on Friday invited tenders for 52,500 tonnes of U.S. yellow No.2 corn by 2.00 p.m. (0500 GMT), traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said shipment was set for November 11-30 if from the Pacific Northwest or October 25-November 15 if from the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
